          <span class="package-tier-card-desc">
            Cocktails, whiskey, gin, rum, a champagne tower or a cigar bar &mdash; added
            alongside your bar package.
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="package-menu-note package-menu-note-warning" data-reveal>
        <svg
          width="16"
          height="16"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="1.6"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
        >
          <path d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0Z" />
          <path d="M12 9v4m0 4h.01" />
        </svg>
        <div class="package-menu-note-text">
          <p>
            <b>Beverage pricing needs confirming before this page goes live.</b>
          </p>
          <p>
            The catalogue itself carries no prices. The figures above come from a quote
            Bacchus shared &mdash; &euro;30 and &euro;35 per person for the wine packages,
            and &euro;23 and &euro;12 per person for the full and reduced open bars.
            Bacchus has said pricing is generated internally and varies by season, so
            treat these as one data point rather than a rate card.
          </p>
          <p>
            A corkage fee also applies to wines and spirits brought in. We have not
            published a figure for it here, because the quote states an amount without
            stating whether it is charged per bottle or per person.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

