      {/* Sits OUTSIDE .package-tier-view/.panels deliberately. It used to
           be the last block inside each of the three .package-tier-content
           blocks — byte-identical in all three — which meant it replayed
           the whole tier-switch motion every time: the click path animates
           .package-tier-content wholesale (packageTierFadeIn), and the
           swipe path slid it across with its panel. A descendant can't opt
           out of an ancestor's opacity/transform animation, so the only
           real fix was to lift it out of the animated container. Doing
           that also collapses the three identical copies into one.

           data-reveal (not .package-reveal) so it still fades in once when
           scrolled to, matching .package-stations-note directly below it —
           the tier switcher's own JS never touches [data-reveal] elements,
           which is exactly why it stays put now on every switch. */}
      <div class="package-menu-note" data-reveal>
        <svg
          width="16"
          height="16"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="1.6"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
        >
          <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" />
          <path d="M12 11v5m0-8h.01" />
        </svg>
        <div class="package-menu-note-text">
          <p>
            Menu items may contain or come into contact with allergens — please discuss
            requirements with the Bacchus sales team.
          </p>
          <p>
            BCL is certified Halal by The World Islamic Call Society (Malta Branch). Full
            terms are in the printed catalogue.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="package-stations-note" data-reveal style="--d: 60ms">
        <p>
          Beverage pairs with any format — see all packages on the
          <a href="/weddings#packages" class="link-underline-inline">
            Weddings page
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

